{
  "configuration_id": "config_033",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_032 (multimodal, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, concat) achieved the best validation accuracy (0.688) and F1 (0.659), outperforming the best RNA-only multiprofile model (config_006, 0.653/0.628) by ~3.5 pp. However, the image-only model (config_010, resnet50) was very weak (0.208), suggesting the image modality contributes only a small complementary signal. Question: config_033 is identical to config_032 except fusion changes from concat to weighted. This isolates the fusion strategy and tests whether the image contribution is best captured by equal-weight concatenation or by learned per-modality weighting. If weighted fusion matches or exceeds concat, it indicates the image signal is small and benefits from down-weighting; if concat is clearly better, the modalities are more complementary than the weak image-only score suggests. Why best next experiment: it is a single-variable comparison directly extending the current best result, requiring no new assumptions, and it reduces uncertainty about whether the modest multimodal gain is robust to a different (and potentially more adaptive) fusion mechanism before investing budget in larger changes like a different image encoder."
}

